<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see rain west, sun east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see rain out west and sun down east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see a few showers in the south and central regions with highs of 10 to 17 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see a mix of sun and cloud with a high of 20 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 16 to 21 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
